This artifact is a binary distribution of PJSIP together with several
third-party projects that are statically linked into libpjsua2.so. Each
carries its own terms; the full texts are in META-INF/licenses/ beside this
file.

PJSIP itself is distributed under the GNU General Public License version 2 or
later, and is also available under a commercial licence from Teluu for use in
applications that cannot meet the GPL's terms. See
https://www.pjsip.org/licensing.htm

Statically linked into libpjsua2.so: OpenSSL, Opus, Oboe, libsrtp, libyuv,
the WebRTC AEC and AEC3, Speex and SpeexDSP, GSM 06.10, and iLBC. Several of those
bundle sub-components under their own separate terms -- the WebRTC AEC3 alone
carries Abseil, the Ooura FFT, RNNoise and PFFFT.

Every licence text is reproduced in this artifact and listed at the end of
this file. Read the text rather than any summary of it: the terms are what
the files say, and several of them require this reproduction.

iLBC is a special case worth stating plainly. The sources bundled with PJSIP
are the RFC 3951 reference implementation and carry only "Copyright (C) The
Internet Society (2004). All Rights Reserved" -- no grant of any kind. That
implementation was relicensed under the 3-clause BSD licence in 2011, after
Google acquired Global IP Solutions, and has since been distributed on those
terms as part of the WebRTC project. LICENSE.ilbc is that text.

One component is deliberately absent:

  libresample   LGPL 2.1. Static linking would place a relink obligation on
                every application shipping this artifact, so Speex's
                resampler is used instead.

Audio and video codecs provided by the Android platform through MediaCodec are
not part of this artifact and are covered by the terms of the device they run
on.
